 [{\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Administrative coverage is the total number of doses given to the target population, divided by the estimated target population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"A measles outbreak is laboratory confirmed when 3 or more laboratory-confirmed measles IgM-positive cases occur in a health facility or district in a month\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Confirmed incidence is derived from cases confirmed in laboratory testing for measles-specific IgM antibodies, and reported to AFRO.\"}, {\"loc\": \"table 1\", \"q\": \"Reported measles vaccination coverage is the proportion of children aged 9--12 months who have received MCV1.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}